Z||000010||Mach10||05-01-2001||08:16 PM||||I work with some rice-primate who owns a "done up" Honda CRX/Del-sol. He's butchered the body panels, nothing is stock except the roof. A HUGE spoiler on the back  5" exhaust tip, and "Street Fighters" on the window, along with any number of japanese decals on the sides. He's got a white fire-extinguisher proudly mounted on the A-pillar on the passenger's side. Filters and coils abound under the hood. Probably boasts 100HP! Oh, He's got a bunch of gauges on the driver's side a-pillar and a huge yellow shift light... TOO BAD IT'S AN AUTO!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000011||JSocha||05-01-2001||09:37 PM||||A kid here in town a few years back, with the actual last name "Duck" had for a hood ornament an actual stuffed duck with lights down the center of the hood (looked like the duck was in a nuclear plant and its cr*p was glowing).  Of all things it was nicknamed the "Duck Mobile" cause the vehicle itself was a boat of a car, hand painted with a paint brush...two tone.<P>Reason why he did it?  He wanted it to be unique and stand out at the parties to which it did.<P>At his graduation party, somebody stole his "Duck" for a keepsake of all things and replaced it apparently with a nice, trophy Dear Head!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
